WEBVTT

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:03.730
"Urgent!
Part-timer Wanted"
"Serving customers" "Shelf stocking and ordering products" "No experience necessary"

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:03.730
I guess I do need someone, don't I...

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:07.230
Even if it's just while I'm at school...

00:00:08.190 --> 00:00:10.230
But I don't know...

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:16.950
Do we even have that kind of money?

00:00:16.950 --> 00:00:19.370
Excuse me.

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:21.000
Welco-- Wha--?!

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:24.620
Greets! You must be the manager!

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:27.880
Huh? Err... What?!

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:31.370
Please let me work here!

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:33.010
Who are you?

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:06.270
"Resume"
"Hajime Owari"

00:02:03.760 --> 00:02:06.850
Let's see... Miss Hajime 
Owari... 20 years old.

00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:09.850
What?! You dropped out
of such a famous university?!

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:12.230
Why did you quit school?

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:14.360
Well... I had my reasons...

00:02:15.190 --> 00:02:18.740
You have certifications, too, so you
should be able to find a better employer.

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:21.280
Well...

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:24.540
The interview suddenly started.

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:27.080
But I'm lucky in a sense!

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:29.790
But why our shop...?

00:02:29.790 --> 00:02:31.290
"Work History"
"November 2017, Worked part-time at
Towns Holdings Kashigahama Branch (customer Service)" "November 2017, Left job for personal reasons"

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:30.990
Hm?

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:34.630
About your one previous job here...

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:37.420
Well... I debated whether
I should put it in there or not...

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:40.800
Yes, I was working at that
convenience store up until yesterday.

00:02:41.340 --> 00:02:42.800
What...? What?!

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:47.520
Well... It was just recently that
that store opened, wasn't it?

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:48.810
You already quit?

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:53.060
Err... Well... I was... fired.

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:53.810
Fired?!

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:58.330
They gave me back my resume and
told me that I didn't have to come back.

00:02:59.320 --> 00:03:01.070
"Four-eyes"       "Not necessary"

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:03.650
This resume...! She reused it?!

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:09.120
Well... I didn't really 
fit in with that group.

00:03:09.580 --> 00:03:11.170
Didn't fit in...

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:12.090
Ah!

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:14.880
The job magazine...

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:16.500
This person!

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:17.560
Ahh...

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.170
That's me.

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:23.220
The only person who didn't seem to fit in!

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:25.430
But it was really tough, y'know!

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:27.220
--Welcome!
--That manager gives a nickname to everyone!

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:28.890
--Welcome!
--That manager gives a nickname to everyone!

00:03:28.890 --> 00:03:30.390
Welcome!

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:32.390
Welcome!

00:03:32.600 --> 00:03:35.940
Wonderful! You guys are already crewmates!

00:03:36.320 --> 00:03:38.900
Why don't we use nicknames
to make things friendly?!

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:40.780
Mikimoto, your nickname is Micky!

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:41.990
Wow!

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:43.530
Motoki, yours is Mokkun!

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:44.570
Whoa!

00:03:44.570 --> 00:03:45.950
Itagaki, yours is Itacchi!

00:03:45.950 --> 00:03:47.450
All right!

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:49.660
Hajime Owari!

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:52.290
Yours is... Four-eyes!

00:03:53.420 --> 00:03:55.920
So mine was Four-eyes...

00:03:56.210 --> 00:03:58.090
What's with the different naming for you?!

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:01.670
Why didn't he shorten your last name
to make it catchy like with the others?!

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:04.430
Plus, "Four-eyes"? Who says that these days?

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:08.720
Right?! It's not like
my glasses stand out! Right?

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:11.180
Well... Um... They kind of do.

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:13.940
Wait, that's not really 
the problem here, is it?!

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:15.440
Y-Yeah...

00:04:15.900 --> 00:04:19.190
But you got fired just
because you didn't fit in?

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:21.950
Oh, that has nothing to do with it.

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:25.490
It's hard to tell you this...
but I was a bit late.

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:28.490
Late? If it's once in a 
while, our shop will--

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:32.000
I was late... every single day
during my training period.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:34.500
What...? Every single day?

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:38.250
Well... Thing is, getting up in
the morning is hella diffi-- Ah!

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:40.250
I mean...

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:44.760
Everything's A-OK!
I'll totally be on time! I swear!

00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:47.760
So... um... please!

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:50.810
I see... Now I get it...

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:54.520
She came here as a last resort
because no one else would hire her.

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:57.980
Well, thanks for coming. I'll let you know
the results later via email or something.

00:04:57.980 --> 00:04:59.770
Hold on a sec!

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:02.900
I know you're trying to get me to leave,
but I'm not having it!

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:05.490
Also, I don't have a phone.

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:10.240
Please! I can't take being
turned down at another interview!

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:12.700
I can't even pay the rent,
so I'm totally screwed!

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:15.680
This minimum wage job is my last chance!

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:18.040
Minimum wage...

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:20.610
To tell you the truth, I was evicted...

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:23.550
By the way, I've been wondering
for a while now, but...

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:25.590
...you<i> are</i> the manager here, right?

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:29.180
Oh, actually, my dad is the manager.

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:30.600
I'm still 15, so...

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:31.560
Fifteen?!

00:05:31.970 --> 00:05:35.310
The two of us were running the shop together,
but he was hospitalized.

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:38.060
So we need someone here during the day.

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:42.320
What...? What?!

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:45.570
That means you live by yourself...

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:48.820
You have an unused room...

00:05:49.660 --> 00:05:50.320
What?

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:54.430
Please let me live and work here!

00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:56.330
What?!

00:05:56.580 --> 00:06:01.340
Then I won't be late for work and
I won't have to worry about where to live!

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:05.340
W-Well, but that's all for <i>your</i> benefit,
isn't it, Ms. Owari?

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:07.010
You can call me Hajime!

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:08.340
Are you trying to cozy up to me?!

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:13.180
Then why don't we do this?

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:17.690
If you let me live here, that's all I want,
so my wages can all go towards the rent.

00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:18.850
What...? What?!

00:06:19.230 --> 00:06:21.860
I-Is this some sort of a trap...? What?

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:23.860
Are you really sure?!

00:06:23.860 --> 00:06:27.110
"Shikada Dagashi"

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:26.220
Lookin' forward to it!

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:29.110
And so, and so...

00:06:32.280 --> 00:06:33.120
Excuse me...

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:35.620
Hajime...?

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:44.130
Could you... get up now?

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:45.880
And...

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:48.820
...why are you sleeping here?

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:54.220
Well, I did tell you that I'm late
like <i>all</i> the time, right?

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:57.890
So I slept here in order not to be late
on my first day at least.

00:06:58.520 --> 00:07:00.140
But in the shop?!

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:03.110
Wait, "on the first day <i>at least</i>"?

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:06.820
Six o'clock?! In the evening?!

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:08.290
No, in the morning.

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:15.160
I got up early so that I can explain what
you'll be doing before I leave for school.

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:19.660
You're a student, huh?
Mm-hmm, school uniforms sure are nice.

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:22.040
You sound like a middle-aged man.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:25.100
Hey, do you have a girl you like?

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:26.670
Ah... let's see...

00:07:26.670 --> 00:07:29.380
Come on, you can tell me!

00:07:29.380 --> 00:07:31.800
I'll start by explaining 
what's on this shelf.

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:34.930
Stack Umai-bou and Maken Gumi
in two layers each.

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:38.680
For Oyatsu Calpas and Dice Caramel,
there's more in the back.

00:07:40.230 --> 00:07:41.190
What's wrong?

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:45.690
I got what I need to do...
but there are so many kinds of <i>dagashi</i>...

00:07:46.020 --> 00:07:50.440
I've only been to a <i>dagashi </i>shop
once or twice, when I was a child.

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:52.820
There are actually people like that?

00:07:52.820 --> 00:07:54.780
What?! Come on, that's harsh!

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:58.080
Well, it may be true that most people
have more experience than me,

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:00.580
but I'm definitely not a rare case!

00:08:00.580 --> 00:08:01.680
Okay...

00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:05.710
Then does it mean that you
haven't eaten much <i>dagashi</i>?

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:08.350
Hmm... I guess so, yeah.

00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:12.010
"Was hiring her really the right decision?"

00:08:12.050 --> 00:08:14.550
I... I... I have! I have!

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:16.220
I thought I saw it around here...

00:08:16.220 --> 00:08:20.270
Here it is! I totally bought
this one all the time!

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:21.230
"Chocoball [Peanut]"

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:21.430
Kyoro-<i>chan</i>!

00:08:21.430 --> 00:08:23.560
Whoa! Chocoball!

00:08:23.560 --> 00:08:26.230
Just like the name suggests,
it's a ball-shaped chocolate snack.

00:08:26.230 --> 00:08:30.230
"Chocoball [Peanut]"

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:28.520
It's one of the biggest players in snacks.

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:31.570
One selling point is the variety of flavors,
including caramel and strawberry.

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:33.490
"Chocoball [Peanut]"
"Chocoball [Strawberry]"      "Chocoball [Caramel]"

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:33.490
The most common flavor is peanut.

00:08:33.820 --> 00:08:38.120
To think a snack like Chocoball
caught your eye... I'm impressed!

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:39.240
Right?!

00:08:39.240 --> 00:08:42.500
Ah... But what I really wanted...

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:43.040
"Beak"

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:44.750
...wasn't the snack itself,
but the can of toys you'd get

00:08:43.040 --> 00:08:47.380
"Gold"                 "Silver"

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:47.380
by sending in one gold ticket
or five silver tickets.

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:51.130
The can of toys over Chocoball...

00:08:52.210 --> 00:08:54.800
"The can of toys over the snack
when she works at a <i>dagashi</i> shop..."
"Was hiring her really the right decision...??"

00:08:54.930 --> 00:08:57.550
Sh-Shoot!

00:08:57.550 --> 00:08:59.050
A <i>dagashi </i>shop would want its workers

00:08:59.050 --> 00:09:02.730
to be more interested in the snacks
themselves rather than toys, I guess?

00:09:02.730 --> 00:09:06.190
And yet, once again I didn't stop
to consider other people's thoughts

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:09.610
and just rambled on about what I like.

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:13.610
I'm gonna get fired again!

00:09:14.450 --> 00:09:16.030
Miss Hajime Owari...

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:17.610
H-He used my full name...!

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:23.290
I'm collecting them, too!
I've collected four silver angel tickets so far!

00:09:23.290 --> 00:09:25.370
Oh, I'm so relieved!

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:28.310
Wait, four tickets?! That's amazing!

00:09:28.960 --> 00:09:33.630
I actually found a Chocoball
can of toys at a thrift shop one time.

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:34.260
What?!

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:38.390
On that day, I had a job interview,

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:41.510
but I wanted it so badly,
even though buying one felt like cheating.

00:09:42.470 --> 00:09:43.520
And...?

00:09:43.520 --> 00:09:50.730
"Thrift Shop"

00:09:44.220 --> 00:09:47.600
I debated all day, but 
ended up not buying it.

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:50.730
Not only that, I skipped the interview, too.
It was a total disaster.

00:09:50.730 --> 00:09:52.520
You missed out on both?!

00:09:52.980 --> 00:09:57.150
I know, right? If I had at least
gotten the can of toys...

00:09:57.150 --> 00:10:00.740
Seriously?! Getting a job is more important!

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:05.540
But because I wasn't able to get a job then,
I can work here now like this.

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:07.040
So it was for the best.

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:11.040
W-Well, if that's how you feel, that's good.

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:13.840
Ah, by the way, did you know this...?

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:18.510
Kyoro-<i>chan</i> looks like just
an ordinary cute illustration,

00:10:15.340 --> 00:10:19.430
"Chocoball [Peanut]"

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:21.800
but despite the fact that he's looking sideways,
you can see both his eyes...

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:23.550
...just like flounder and halibut.

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:27.180
This design is called cubism.

00:10:27.180 --> 00:10:28.980
It's a crazy expression technique

00:10:28.980 --> 00:10:32.770
where you combine things
from various angles into one picture.

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:35.820
It's a technique started 
by Picasso and others.

00:10:36.110 --> 00:10:38.320
Isn't it kinda crazy?

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:38.820
"It bugs me... that I didn't know that!"

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:41.910
Then do you know this...?

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:46.330
The mascot character for Chocoball
wasn't originally Kyoro-<i>chan</i>.

00:10:46.910 --> 00:10:49.210
It was totally a different
anime character, and...

00:10:49.210 --> 00:10:50.170
Manager...

00:10:50.170 --> 00:10:51.460
Hm?

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:52.250
Is it okay...?

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:53.000
What?

00:10:53.000 --> 00:10:53.840
Ahh!

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:56.930
Well then, look after the shop, okay?!

00:10:57.970 --> 00:11:00.340
See you later!

00:11:00.510 --> 00:11:02.850
Be careful!

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:10.190
"Hajime Owari, Chocoball, and..."

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:09.780
Whaattt?!

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:16.510
"Next time"
"Roll Candy, High Eight Chocolate, and..."

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:11.080
Next time. "Roll Candy,
High Eight Chocolate, and..."

00:12:11.080 --> 00:12:14.630
Unforgivable! Who the hell is that woman?!
